//   - RFC 4180 COMMA/DQUOTE profile (`CsvDialectRfc4180`); not a tunable multi-dialect surface here.
//   - `CsvRow` / `CsvDocument` (+ `CsvHeaderPresence`): pre-ruling tabular carriers (`Nat` width + `List<String>` per row); rectangularity operator-pending (Deferred (2)).
//   - Future `csv_parse` / `csv_emit` — Deferred (1); `Outcome<…>` seam (json.dag #3184 / DECISIONS I).
//
// Consumes: std/node.dag, std/diagnostic.dag, std/collection.dag, std/text.dag
//
// Status: scaffold — fill per TASKS.md T-4.6
// Brief: see BRIEF_TEMPLATE.md; this file's I/O contract is the immutable contract
// for the worker. Splitting this file requires explicit operator ratification.
//
// ─── HEADER RECONCILE (operator directive, vivid-carp-207, dashboard msg_3499949b-8d4e-4826-a51d-05b9e1757775, 2026-05-17) ───
// In-PR de-prose: comment volume reduced; carriers unchanged.
//
// Seams: C5 anchor pin; mirror json `Outcome` fail-closed parse+emit; no bodiless `fn` (DECISIONS PARSE-1).
// Immut. header `Result` / total-`String` emit ↔ `Outcome` reconcile per json.dag #3184 class (Deferred (1)).

module v4.extdeps.formats.csv


import v4.std.nat { Nat }


// CsvDialect — RFC 4180 §2 nullary witness (fixed COMMA/DQUOTE grammar).
// Anchor: https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc4180#section-2
// Practice 4: GREEN — one profile per arm; new profiles = new arm or sibling file.
type CsvDialect
  = CsvDialectRfc4180 {}


// CsvHeaderPresence — optional header row (P2 explicit sum, not `Option<Row>`).
// Anchor: https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc4180#section-2
// Practice 4: GREEN.
type CsvHeaderPresence
  = HeaderPresent { row: CsvRow }
  | HeaderAbsent


// CsvRow — one logical record = ordered field list (`Row` in immutable header).
// Anchor: https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc4180#section-2
// Practice 4: N/A (Conj). Rectangularity vs `width`: Deferred (2).
type CsvRow {
  fields: List<String>,
}


// CsvDocument — header + body + `width: Nat` (counting carrier; strict PositiveInt refinements operator-pending).
// Anchor: https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc4180#section-2
// Practice 4: N/A (Conj). Row arity vs `width`: Deferred (2); no false structural rectangularity claim.
type CsvDocument {
  width: Nat,
  header: CsvHeaderPresence,
  records: List<CsvRow>,
}


// Deferred — TRACKED SCAFFOLD (🟡).
//
// (1) `csv_parse` / `csv_emit` — RFC 4180 §2 on std/text; `CsvDialectRfc4180`; `Outcome` fail-closed both ways (json.dag #3184).
//   (a) doc — this block. (b) bounds — symbols absent here. (c) trigger — std/text lands ⇒ ops + emit validation (Unicode/CRLF/quotes) + CSV consistency rules **after** (2) where applicable.
//
// (2) Operator **csv-rectangularity ruling** — rectangularity, width rules, ragged rows, header/body arity, parse on mismatch: deferred to named ruling + substrate; no worker disposition. Trigger: ruling + substrate ⇒ wire Deferred (1) `Outcome` ops.
